-- title:
--   Diamond invariance of the Σ^∞ condition on the pole chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero level $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and a witness $hj$ that $jqModC\ \mathbb{Q}$ lies in the intermediate field $qExpFunctionFieldC\ \mathbb{Q}\ \top$ of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$; let $\mathfrak{P}$ be a model datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, let $\rho : R\,p \to A$ be a ring map with $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ after $\rho$ equal to the structure map $R\,p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $\kappa$ be an $R\,p$-algebra whose structure map is $\rho$ followed by the residue map. Write $O = chartAlgInf\ p\ (\Gamma_M\,M\,H)\ hj$ for the pole chart, the $R\,p$-subalgebra of elements of the $q$-expansion function field integral over $R\,p[j^{-1}]$. Let $red : O \to \kappa((q))$ be a ring map such that $red\,b$ is the coefficientwise image under $\kappa$-reduction of any Laurent series $y$ over $R\,p$ whose image in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ is the $q$-expansion of $b$. Let $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ and let $\sigma$ be an $R\,p$-algebra automorphism of $O$ with $\iota_\infty$ followed by the diamond $\mathfrak{P}.dia\ d$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}\sigma$ followed by $\iota_\infty$. Then for every point $z$ of $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_{R\,p} O)$, the ideal generated by $\ker red$ via the right inclusion $O \to \kappa \otimes_{R\,p} O$ is contained in the prime of $z$ if and only if it is contained in the prime of the image of $z$ under the map on points induced by $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{id}_\kappa \otimes \sigma)$.
--
--   On the pole chart of the special fibre, containment of the ideal generated by $\ker red$ in the prime of a point expresses that the point lies on the component through the cusp $\infty$; the statement says that this condition is invariant under the diamond automorphism $\langle d \rangle$ read algebraically as $\sigma$. It is the scheme-theoretic-to-algebraic transport step used in showing that diamond operators preserve the Gauss valuation ring, and is cited in the analysis of $q$-expansions of diamond translates at level $M$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_map_ker_le_asIdeal_iff_map_ker_le_spec_map_tensor_asIdeal.lean

